---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const title = "DTI Income Documentation Checklist";
const description =
  "How to document income for DTI calculations, including pay stubs, tax records, and variable income notes. Educational use only.";

const lastUpdated = "2026-02-08";
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonicalPath="/guides/dti-income-documentation-checklist" lastUpdated={lastUpdated}>
  <section class="card hero">
    <span class="pill">Guide</span>
    <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/">Home</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <a href="/guides">Guides</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span aria-current="page">Income documentation</span>
    </nav>
    <h1>DTI income documentation checklist</h1>
    <p>
      DTI relies on gross monthly income that can be verified. This checklist helps you align calculator inputs with the documents
      lenders typically review so your ratio reflects what underwriting will see.
    </p>
    <div class="btn-row">
      <a class="btn" href="/topics/debt-to-income">DTI topic hub</a>
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/calculators/debt-to-income-calculator">DTI calculator</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/guides/dti-variable-income-averaging">Variable income averaging</a>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">DTI inputs to verify</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Gross monthly income from documented sources.</li>
      <li>Housing payment (PITI + HOA + PMI if applicable).</li>
      <li>Required minimum payments for other debts.</li>
      <li>Any lender-specific rules for student loans or deferred debt.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Core checklist</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Recent pay stubs showing year-to-date income.</li>
      <li>Two years of W-2s or tax returns (if requested).</li>
      <li>Employment verification or offer letter for new roles.</li>
      <li>Bonus or commission documentation if it is consistent.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="grid" style="margin-top:18px">
    <div class="card section prose col-6">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0">W-2 income</h2>
      <p class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0">
        Use your stable base pay converted to a monthly amount. If overtime or bonuses are irregular, do not rely on a single strong
        month unless it is documented and consistent.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="card section prose col-6">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0">Variable income</h2>
      <p class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0">
        For commissions or bonuses, lenders often use a multi-year average. Keep a simple record of the period used so the DTI input
        matches the documentation.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Co-borrower documentation</h2>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0">
      If you are adding a co-borrower to improve DTI, include their income documents and also their required debts. The ratio only
      improves if the added income outweighs the added debt payments.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Self-employed income notes</h2>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0">
      Self-employed income is usually based on net income after expenses. Gather recent tax returns, year-to-date P&L statements,
      and any required add-back documentation before using a monthly income figure.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Income conversion tips</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Hourly wages: multiply by average hours per week and by 52, then divide by 12.</li>
      <li>Biweekly pay: multiply by 26 to get annual, then divide by 12.</li>
      <li>Monthly pay: use the gross monthly number on the statement.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Keep a simple income worksheet</h2>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0">
      Save the sources you used for each income line (pay stubs, tax returns, or P&L). When you rerun the DTI calculator, you can
      update only the lines that changed without rechecking everything.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Next steps</h2>
    <div class="btn-row" style="margin-top:10px">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/calculators/debt-to-income-calculator">Run DTI with documented income</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/guides/dti-self-employed-income">Self-employed income</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/guides/dti-co-borrower-impacts">Co-borrower impacts</a>
    </div>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:12px 0 0">Educational use only. Not financial advice.</p>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:12px 0 0; font-size:13px">Last updated: 2026-02-08</p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>


